mum said , " let 's buy this one . it will replace your pale skirt . "

mary smiled and said yes . she was so happy she had found the perfect skirt to replace the pale one . from then on she always felt beautiful when she danced . one day , there was a little boy called lee . he found a big bowl of dough in the kitchen and he was so excited . he quickly grabbed a spoon and started to stir it . then he added some sugar and stirred again .

suddenly , his mom came in to the kitchen and said , " lee , what are you doing ? " lee said , " mommy , i am making dough . " his mom replied , " yes , but dough needs to be washed before you can eat it . " lee 's face turned sad , but he quickly remembered that his mom always gives him good advice .

so , he washed the dough and found it tasted much better and looked brighter . from that day on , lee always remembered to wash whatever he wanted to eat .

the moral of the story is to remember to always wash things before you eat them . once upon a time , there was a little girl who loved to write . she would write all kinds of things , like stories and poems . one of the poems was so incredible that she wanted to keep it forever . so she decided to bury it .

she went outside and found a spot in her garden that was perfect for burying her poem . she put a big spoonful of dirt on top and patted it down . then she said goodbye to her poem and whispered , " i hope nobody finds it ! "

