mom and dad come over and praise tom . they help him unhook the fish and put it in a bucket . they tell him he can keep it or let it go .

tom thinks for a moment . he likes the fish , but he also likes the lake . he decides to let the fish go . he holds it gently and puts it back in the water . he says goodbye to the fish and thanks it for the fun .

lily watches tom and thinks he is kind . she wants to be kind too . she hopes the fish will be happy and safe . she hopes she will catch a fish and let it go too . she holds her rod and waits and watches . she is enthusiastic . anna and ben were playing with their toys in the living room . they liked to pretend they were on a stage and sing songs for their mom and dad . they had a big box that they used as a microphone and a curtain that they pulled to hide and show themselves .

one day , they decided to sing a song about the fridge . they thought the fridge was very funny because it made noises and had food inside . they sang :

the fridge is big and white it keeps our food cold and bright sometimes it goes hum and sometimes it goes beep we like to open it and take a peek

they pulled the curtain and waited for their mom and dad to applaud . but they did not hear any clapping . they looked and saw that their mom and dad were not in the living room . they were in the kitchen , making lunch .

anna and ben felt sad . they wanted their mom and dad to see their show and tell them they were good . they walked to the kitchen and saw their mom and dad looking at something on the counter . it was a cake . a big , ugly cake .

their mom and dad had tried to bake a cake for their anniversary , but it did not turn out well . it was lumpy and burned and had too much frosting . their mom and dad looked sad too .

