he turned around and walked back to his crib . he climbed in and pulled the blanket over him . he felt sad and lonely . he wished he could sleep with his mom and dad .

but then he remembered what his dad had said . he was a big boy now . he needed to learn to sleep by himself . it was good for him . his mom and dad loved him , but they also needed their space and their rules . he had to respect them .

he closed his eyes and tried to think of happy things . he thought of his toys , his friends , his pets , his books . he thought of how his mom and dad would hug him and kiss him in the morning . he thought of how proud they would be of him for sleeping in his crib .

he felt a little better . he smiled and fell asleep .

the moral of the story is : respect your parents ' space and rules , and learn to be independent . anna and ben like to play in the woods . they find a trail with many leaves and sticks . they run and jump on the trail . they see orange flowers and orange birds . they are happy .

but then they hear a loud roar . they stop and look around . they see a big bear . the bear is angry . it has orange fur and orange eyes . it wants to scare anna and ben .

anna and ben are scared . they run away from the bear . they do not look back . they find their mom and dad . they hug them and tell them about the bear .

mom and dad are surprised . they say the bear is rare . they say it is a sun bear . they say it is not very dangerous . they say they are proud of anna and ben for being brave .

anna and ben are glad . they are safe and loved . they do not want to see the sun bear again . they want to play on a different trail . they want to see blue flowers and blue birds . they are happy . lily and ben are friends . they like to play in the park . one day , they see a big slide . lily wants to go on the slide , but ben is scared .

