she carried him to their house . she put him in his bed . she gave him some water . she sang him a song . he felt better . he felt sleepy .

he closed his eyes . he dreamed of the storm . but he did not like it anymore . he liked his mother . and his house . and his bed . he was safe . he was happy . sam was a boy who liked to play with his toys . he had many toys , but his favorite was a big , hairy bear . he called him bobo . he hugged bobo every night and took him everywhere .

one day , sam went to the park with his mom and bobo . he saw other kids playing with balls , bikes , and dolls . he wanted to play with them , but he did not want to share bobo . he thought bobo was too special and he was afraid someone would take him or hurt him .

he saw a girl with a pretty wrap on her head . it was pink and shiny and had flowers on it . sam wanted to have it . he ran to the girl and grabbed the wrap . he put it on bobo 's head and said , " now bobo is prettier than you ! "

the girl started to cry . she said , " that 's my wrap ! my grandma gave it to me ! give it back ! " she tried to pull the wrap from bobo , but sam held on tight . they both pulled and pulled , until the wrap tore in half .

