she and her mom made a new pastry for her dad , with more blueberries . they baked it and put it on a plate . they wrote a note that said , " for dad , from anna and mom . we love you . "

they left the plate on the table and waited for dad to come home . they hoped he would like their special pastry . they knew he would like it more than the regular ones . lily likes to play with her drum . she has a big drum that is black and red . she likes to hit the drum with her sticks and make loud noises . she thinks it is fun .

one day , lily is playing with her drum in the garden . she sees a bird on a tree . the bird is blue and yellow . it has a long tail . lily thinks the bird is pretty . she wants to talk to the bird .

" hello , bird ! " lily says . " do you like my drum ? "

the bird looks at lily and her drum . it opens its beak and makes a sound . the sound is like the drum . it goes " boom boom boom " .

lily is surprised . she laughs . " you can make drum sounds , bird ! " she says . " you are clever ! "

the bird makes more drum sounds . it goes " boom boom boom , tap tap tap " . lily copies the bird . she hits her drum and goes " boom boom boom , tap tap tap " . they make music together .

lily and the bird are happy . they play with the drum until the sun goes down . they are friends . tom and sam were brothers who liked to play in the woods . they had a small hut made of sticks and leaves , where they kept their toys and snacks . one day , they found a shiny axe near a big tree . tom wanted to take it , but sam said no .

" that is not ours . it belongs to someone else . maybe it is the woodcutter 's axe . he needs it to chop wood and make money . we should leave it here , " sam said .

" but it is so shiny and sharp . i want to try it . maybe i can chop some wood too . it will be fun , " tom said .

he did not listen to sam and took the axe . he ran to a small tree and swung the axe hard . but the axe was too heavy for him and he missed the tree . he hit his foot instead and cried out loud .

" ow , ow , ow ! it hurts , it hurts ! " tom wailed .

sam ran to him and saw blood on his foot . he was scared and worried . he tore a piece of his shirt and wrapped it around tom 's foot . he helped him to stand up and limp back to their hut .

they saw the woodcutter coming to the woods . he was tall and strong , with a big beard and a hat . he looked angry and confused . he saw his axe on the ground and picked it up .

" who took my axe ? who did this ? " he shouted .

sam and tom were afraid . they hid in their hut and hoped he would not see them . but the woodcutter heard their voices and walked to their hut . he opened the door and saw them inside .

" did you take my axe ? did you hurt yourself with it ? " he asked .

tom was ashamed and sorry . he nodded and said , " yes , sir . i am sorry . i wanted to play with it . but i hit my foot and it hurts a lot . please do n't be mad at me . "

the woodcutter sighed and shook his head . he said , " you are lucky you did not hurt yourself more . you should not take things that are not yours . you should listen to your brother . he was right . this axe is not a toy . it is a tool . it is dangerous for children . you could have cut yourself or someone else . you could have damaged the trees or the animals . you should respect other people 's property and work . you should be careful and responsible . do you understand ? "

tom nodded and said , " yes , sir . i understand . i am sorry . i will not do it again . "

the woodcutter smiled and said , " that is good . i forgive you . but you should also say sorry to your brother . he tried to stop you and help you . he is a good brother . you should be thankful and kind to him . "

tom turned to sam and said , " i am sorry , sam . you were right . i was wrong . thank you for helping me . you are a good brother . i love you . "

sam hugged him and said , " i love you too , tom . i am glad you are okay . let 's go home and tell mom what happened . she will take care of your foot and make you feel better . "

the woodcutter helped them to get out of the hut and gave them some cookies . he said , " go home and be safe . and remember , never play with axes again . "

tom and sam said , " thank you , sir . we will remember . goodbye . "

they waved to him and walked home , holding hands . they learned a lesson that day . they learned to be honest , respectful , and careful . they learned to listen to each other and to their elders . they learned that axes are not toys . ben and mia liked to play with their toy cars . they had many cars of different colors and sizes . they liked to make roads and bridges with blocks and books . sometimes they pretended that their cars could fly or swim .

one day , they found a big box in the garage . it had a picture of a rocket on it . ben and mia were curious . they opened the box and saw many pieces of metal and plastic . they also saw a book with words and pictures . they could not read the words , but they liked the pictures .

they decided to make a rocket with the pieces . they looked at the book and tried to copy the pictures . they used tape and glue to attach the pieces together . they worked hard and had fun . they made a big rocket that looked like the one on the box .

they wanted to see if their rocket could fly . they took it outside and put it on the grass . they saw a red button on the rocket . they thought it was for flying . ben pushed the button and ran away with mia .

the rocket made a loud noise and a bright light . it flew up in the air very fast . ben and mia were amazed and happy . they clapped and cheered . they watched the rocket go higher and higher .

but then something bad happened . the rocket exploded in the air . it made a big boom and a lot of smoke . pieces of the rocket fell down like rain . some of them were hot and burned the grass . some of them were black and gray like ash . ben and mia were scared and sad . they ran back to the garage and hid behind the box .

they heard their mom and dad come outside . they saw the mess and the smoke . they were angry and worried . they asked ben and mia what they did . ben and mia told them the truth . they said they were sorry . they said they wanted to make a rocket and fly .

their mom and dad hugged them and said they were glad they were not hurt . they said they were clever to make a rocket , but they should not play with things they did not understand . they said they should always ask before they use something . they said they should be careful and safe .

ben and mia nodded and said they learned their lesson . they said they would not make a rocket again . they said they would play with their toy cars instead . they said they loved their mom and dad . their mom and dad smiled and said they loved them too . they helped them clean up the mess and the ash . they gave them their toy cars and some cookies . they said they were proud of them for being honest and brave . they said they were sorry for being angry and worried .

ben and mia thanked them and said they were sorry too . they hugged and kissed them . they played with their toy cars and ate their cookies . they were happy and safe . they did not want to make a rocket anymore . they liked their toy cars better . tom was a smart boy who liked to wear his red cap . he always did his best at school and helped his mom and dad at home . he had many friends who liked to play with him and share his toys .

one day , tom was walking to the park with his mom and his cap . he saw a big dog on the street . the dog looked angry and hungry . it barked loudly and ran towards tom . tom was scared and tried to run away , but the dog was faster . it bit tom 's leg and pulled his cap off his head .

tom cried out in pain and fear . his mom ran to him and hugged him . she tried to comfort him and stop the bleeding . she called for help and waited for the ambulance . the dog ran away with tom 's cap in its mouth .

tom was taken to the hospital . he had to get stitches and medicine . he was very sad and hurt . he missed his cap and his friends . he wished the dog had never seen him . he wondered if he would ever feel happy and smart again . he wished he had stayed at home . sara and tom are playing with their toys on the rug . they have cars , dolls , blocks and books . they are having fun and making noises .

