they hold hands and run inside . they take off their coats and boots and play with their toys . they are good friends . they follow the law . and they wait for the rain to stop . once upon a time , there was a swan who loved to shine in the sun . she had beautiful feathers that sparkled in the light . one day , she met a group of ducks who asked her to play with them . the swan was happy to join in , but the ducks did n't like her because she was different . they teased her and said she was n't a real duck .

the swan felt sad , but she did n't let the ducks bring her down . she decided to be independent and play on her own . as she swam in the pond , she saw her reflection in the water and realized that she was special just the way she was . she did n't need to change to fit in with the ducks .

the moral of the story is that it 's important to be true to yourself and not let others make you feel bad for being different . just like the swan , we should shine in our own unique way and be proud of who we are . once upon a time , there was a little girl named lily . she loved to eat candy , especially lollipops . one day , lily went to the candy store with her mom . she saw a big jar of lollipops and asked her mom if she could have one . her mom said yes , so she picked out a red one .

