ben and lily go to the barn . they see a big pile of hay . they have to sort it into smaller piles . one pile for the cows , one pile for the horses , one pile for the sheep , and one pile for the chickens . they start to work . but soon they get bored . they think of a new game . they make hay forts and throw hay at each other . they laugh and have fun .

mom comes to the barn . she sees the hay forts and the hay on the floor . she is not happy . she says , " you did not sort the hay . you made a mess . you have to clean up the barn and sort the hay . then you have to go to your room . no toys and animals for you today . "

ben and lily are sorry . they say , " sorry , mom . we will clean up and sort the hay . we will not play games when we have chores . " mom says , " good . now hurry up and finish . then go to your room and think about what you did . "

ben and lily clean up and sort the hay . they are sad . they wish they had shared and been kind . they go to their room and think about what they did . they say , " we are sorry . we will not fight over toys and animals . we will share and be kind . we love each other . " they hug and make up . they hope mom will forgive them and let them play tomorrow . lily loved to paint . she had many colors and brushes and papers . she liked to make pictures of flowers and animals and houses . sometimes she gave her paintings to her mom and dad and they smiled and hugged her .

one day , lily 's uncle came to visit . he was very big and loud and funny . he made lily laugh with his jokes and faces . he also liked to paint . he had a big bag with many paintings inside . he showed them to lily and her parents . they were very pretty and different . they had shapes and lines and dots and swirls .

lily wanted to paint with her uncle . she asked him if she could . he said yes and smiled . he gave her a paper and a brush and some colors . he told her to paint whatever she wanted . lily was happy . she dipped her brush in the blue and made a big circle . then she dipped it in the yellow and made a smaller circle inside . she made a sun .

her uncle watched her and nodded . he said she was a good painter . he told her to be careful with his paintings . he said they were delicate . lily did not know what that word meant . she asked him . he said it meant they could break or tear easily . he said she had to be gentle with them .

lily understood . she wanted to be gentle with her uncle 's paintings . she liked them . she asked him if she could see them again . he said yes and opened his bag . he took out one painting and showed it to her . it was very colorful and shiny . it had glitter and beads and feathers on it . lily thought it was beautiful . she reached out to touch it .

her uncle stopped her . he said no . he said she could not touch it . he said it was too delicate . he said she could only look at it . lily was sad . she wanted to feel the glitter and the beads and the feathers . she thought they would be soft and smooth and tickly . she did not understand why she could not touch them .

